{
  "title": "Málaga, Spain",
  "indexDescription": "Christmas trip in 2009 to visit Alex in Málaga Spain.",
  "description": "Christmas in Spain — 2009\n\nIn December 2009, our family traveled to Spain to visit Alex, who was spending his junior year of college studying in Málaga. We had three weeks over Christmas break to visit him and explore the country. Málaga was our first stop, followed by a tour of southern Spain, Barcelona and Madrid.\n\nArriving in Málaga\n\nGetting to Málaga took more than 24 hours, and the journey was grueling. Our first night was spent in the historic old town, where narrow streets were too small for cars. We were exhausted and jet-lagged, but sleep was hard to come by.\n\nJust around the corner from our window was a noisy bar. We soon discovered that bars in Spain could stay open until 7:00 a.m.! Then, around 8:00 a.m., the garbage trucks began making their rounds. \n\nExploring Málaga\n\nWe visited Alex in his dorm room and began adjusting to the Spanish way of life, including eating dinner much later than we were used to.\n\nWhile in Málaga, we visited the Picasso Museum and explored the Alcazaba, an ancient Moorish fortress perched on a hillside overlooking the city. We also walked to the top of the hill to take in the views of Málaga.",
